    "updated_at": "2020-12-14T17:29:28Z",
    "body": "This is actually what I arrived at too, but I'm not super happy with it for two reasons: 1) it relies on JavaScript of course, so won't work when JavaScript is disabled, and 2) it relies on a tight coupling with the parent page (meaning anywhere else I might want to use it I have to have the message receiver, and I have to do the kind of double-handling in case the page is ever loaded on its own so that it doesnt postMessage to nothing, etc.)",
